# Quivers in the off-hand; the ammunition slot becomes a second ring slot (server/README.md "Infinite arrows and
# quivers", "Second ring slot"). Owner requests: "Quivers go in the off-hand now." and then "Don't remove the ammo slot.
# Turn it into a second ring slot." Bows and crossbows stay two-handed (every two-handed rule, weapon_styles.lua's
# two-handed speed and damage, the keystones and the class kits see them as before); the one exception is the quiver.
#   * a new weapon type WEAPON_QUIVER (const.h; items.xml weaponType "quiver", written by
#     server/tools/patch_base_archery.py; Lua constant WEAPON_QUIVER = 8; getWeaponName "quiver"). It is no weapon:
#     Player::getWeapon skips it, Player::getShieldAndWeapon counts it as neither shield nor weapon (defense, shielding).
#   * Player::queryAdd, classicEquipmentSlots = false (the Chaos setting): the shield hand takes a quiver while the
#     weapon hand holds a bow or crossbow (a two-handed distance weapon) or nothing; the weapon hand takes a bow or
#     crossbow next to a quiver, and refuses every other weapon while a quiver is in the shield hand. A shield (or a
#     dual-wield blade) next to a launcher is still refused (both hands need to be free). A quiver never goes in the
#     weapon hand. Every equip path asks queryAdd: drag and drop, the equip hotkey (Game::playerEquipItem), a script's
#     addItem / addItemEx with a slot (loadouts, kits), Player::queryDestination; only the login (IOLoginData) skips it,
#     and data/scripts/chaos/archery.lua checks the hands and the second ring slot there.
#   * the second ring slot (CONST_SLOT_AMMO, slot 10): it takes the item types the ring slot takes (slot position
#     ring) and nothing else (the base's "Quiver" name exception goes). MoveEvents::getEvent looks up the ring events
#     for it (slot="ring" in movements.xml), so a ring there gets its abilities, its vocation and level check and its
#     transformation on equip and de-equip (the timed rings) as in the ring slot; Player::getArmor counts it. The equip
#     hotkey of a ring uses the second slot when the first holds another ring and the second is free (or holds that
#     ring: the hotkey takes it off).
#   * classicEquipmentSlots = true is not supported for quivers: a quiver is then a second hand item and is refused
#     next to a two-handed launcher, as before.
# Apply in the server source root after 0001-0022: patch -p1 < 0023-quiver-off-hand.patch, then rebuild.
